|                                                                                |
|    Setup guide                                                                 |
|                                                                                |
|    This guide teaches you to set up, check and run a Velour BBS on             |
|    a Linux host. It is for the sysop. You need a Linux host with               |
|    systemd, root access, a text editor and a telnet client.                    |
|                                                                                |
|    Each section ends with a check of the result. A section refers              |
|    to the specifications that hold its full rules. The BBT guide               |
|    teaches you to write the screens.                                           |
|                                                                                |
|    Parts                                                                       |
|                                                                                |
|      ∙ 1. The program                                                          |
